Subject: [PATCH] tests/e2e: rework MT golden-flow to land within current
 tenant API scope
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The first cut of the golden-flow spec assumed the tenant CRUD routes
accepted the full legacy create body (budget, rate_limit,
provider_configs on VK; budget on team).  In practice the tenant
handlers are minimum-viable:

  CreateTenantVirtualKeyRequest → {name, value?, description?}
  UpdateTenantVirtualKeyRequest → {name?, description?, is_active?}
  CreateTenantTeamRequest       → {id?, name, customer_id?}

So any budget / rate_limit / provider_configs payload silently drops,
leaving the VK with empty provider_configs.  /v1 routing then falls
through to the global model catalog and lands on whichever provider
first claimed `qwen3.6-coder` (in the user's case `qw3`).

Rework the test to drive only what the v1 API supports, and document
the tenant-API gap with a KNOWN GAPS block so a future spec can close
the budget-cap loop once those routes accept the full body.

What the spec now proves end-to-end:

  - login + create tenant on first sign-in (badge + localStorage)
  - custom openai-shaped provider via UI (qwen3-coder Service URL)
  - provider key with model allow-list via UI
  - VK via UI; capture the one-shot secret from the create response
  - warmup unqualified /v1 call materializes the tenant runtime so
    ParseModelString recognizes the custom provider name; subsequent
    qualified `{provider}/{model}` calls land on the tenant provider
  - 5 successful /v1/chat/completions calls against the in-cluster
    qwen3.6-coder
  - log rows render in /workspace/logs (Stage 4 tenant_id stamping)
  - team CRUD via UI

Verified green against the bm k3d cluster — 5/5 calls 200, ~265
tokens consumed.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
